{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothContradiction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothContradiction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothIndexGap","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothRealLadder"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction_at_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction_at_witness","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L213-L255","doc":"**The structural hypotheses are jointly satisfiable.**  `roth_contradiction` concludes `False`,\nso its hypotheses are *supposed* to be jointly unsatisfiable — which means vacuity is not the risk.\nThe risk is that some **structural** subset is already inconsistent, making the theorem true for a\nreason having nothing to do with Roth.  This rules that out by supplying every structural argument\nat the parameters of `index_le_rothBound_witness` (`m = 2`, `p = q = 1`, `F = 10`, `a = 1`,\n`r = (1,1)`, `H = (1024,1024)`, `P = 1`, `κ = 1024`, `α = 1024`, `G = 0`), leaving exactly the two\nnumeric conditions as hypotheses.\n\n⚠ It does **not** show the collision fires.  At `μ = ν = 0` both remaining hypotheses are false —\n`hlog` because `taylorConst > 1` makes its left side positive while its right side is `0`, and\n`hgap` because `c₂² · 1 = 25` is not below `0`.  They must be false somewhere, or `False` would be\nderivable from satisfiable hypotheses.  Both holding at once needs `μ ≈ m(½−ε)` from step 1 and\n`K ≈ (2+δ)L` from an approximation exponent above `2`, which is Roth's inequality and is what a\nparameter record has to deliver — not something a small witness can exhibit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L179-L211","doc":"**Step 4.**  Steps 2 and 3 in one place: the Taylor lower bound and Roth's Lemma's upper bound\non the same index, contradicting each other as soon as the numeric hypotheses hold.\n\nThe last two hypotheses are the whole of the parameter bookkeeping — `hlog` is Roth's inequality\n(sizes on the left, index gap times approximation exponent on the right) and `hgap` says the ratio\n`p/q` that `Γ_m` supplies is smaller than `(ν/c_m)^{2^{m−1}}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.algebraMap_int_rat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.algebraMap_int_rat","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L170-L177","doc":"The unique ring hom `ℤ → ℚ`, under its two names — step 3 states its conclusion with\n`algebraMap`, step 2 with `Int.castRingHom`.\n\n⚠ **Not load-bearing.**  I wrote this expecting to need it and used it to bridge the two\nstatements; deleting the bridging rewrite and rebuilding shows the file still compiles, so the two\nunify definitionally.  Kept as a recorded check — the claim \"composing the halves surfaced an\ninterface mismatch\" was mine and was wrong, and the lemma is the evidence for the correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.false_of_le_index_of_rothBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.false_of_le_index_of_rothBound","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L155-L168","doc":"**The collision.**  A lower bound `ν` and Roth's Lemma's upper bound cannot both hold once\n`c_m^{2^{m−1}}·(p/q)` drops below `ν^{2^{m−1}}`.  Everything else in Roth's theorem exists to make\nthat one inequality available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.log_taylorConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.log_taylorConst","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L118-L147","doc":"**What a parameter choice has to beat, term by term.**  `log(taylorConst)` splits into four\nnamed costs: the box count (twice — once for `P`'s support, once for its translate), the height of\n`P`, the translation cost `(2B)^{Σr}`, and the peeling cost `2^{Σr}`.\n\nWriting it out is the point of the exercise.  In the additive form of Roth's inequality the whole\nleft side is `2·log(box) + log H + Σr·log(4B) + Σ_h r_h·log q_h`, and every one of those terms\nscales with `Σ_h r_h` except `log H`.  So the normalisation cannot be one-sided: `r_h·log q_h ≥ L`\nalone bounds the right side from below but leaves `Σ_h r_h·log q_h` on the left unbounded above,\nand a parameter record that carries only the lower bound cannot discharge this.  That is a\nconstraint on the record, discovered by writing the decomposition rather than by assuming it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.le_index_rational_of_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.le_index_rational_of_log","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L84-L116","doc":"**Step 2, with its numeric hypothesis in additive form.**  The left side is the auxiliary\npolynomial's size plus the denominators' size; the right side is the index gap times the\napproximation exponent.  That is Roth's inequality as it is stated in prose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.log_prod_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.log_prod_pow","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L75-L82","doc":"`log ∏_h q_h^{r_h} = ∑_h r_h·log q_h` — the denominators' contribution, in the currency the\nnormalisation `r_h·log q_h ≈ L` is stated in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mul_exp_neg_lt_one_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mul_exp_neg_lt_one_div","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**The additive form of the numeric hypothesis.**  `C·e^{−g} < 1/D` is `log C + log D < g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.taylorConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.taylorConst","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothContradiction.lean#L57-L62","doc":"The constant `le_index_rational_of_taylor` multiplies `e^{−K(μ−ν)}` by: the box count twice\n(once for the support of `P`, once for the support of its translate), the height, and the two\npeeling factors. ","signatureChunk":0}]}